---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="About">
  <main class="page-block">
    <h1>About</h1>
    <p>
      Project Vibrare is a personal study notebook and archive about music: theory, analysis and arranging. It
      brings together notes, small interactive tools, reference lists and a collection of arrangements in one place.
    </p>

    <h2 class="section-title">What is here</h2>
    <ul class="about-list">
      <li>
        <strong>Theory.</strong> Notes on tonal harmony, partimento (the bass-pattern teaching method of the
        eighteenth-century Italian conservatories), counterpoint and jazz. Some of these sections are still being
        written.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Analysis.</strong> The preludes and fugues of Bach's <em>Well-Tempered Clavier</em> with their BWV
        numbers and keys, and the soundtracks of the numbered Touhou Project games, Th06 to Th20.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Tools.</strong> Interval, scale and chord calculators, and an interactive circle of fifths that
        draws the shape of a chord. Notes are spelled the way a musician would write them.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Works.</strong> Arrangements, sorted by kind: anime, flute, concert band, Ghibli, Touhou Project,
        Vocaloid, VTubers, commissions and more.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Glossary and Resources.</strong> Terms used across the site, and books, websites and software for
        further study.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="section-title">About the sources</h2>
    <p>
      Facts are checked against more than one source where possible. The Touhou track lists, for example, come from
      Japanese Wikipedia and are cross-checked against two other community databases, and corrections found that
      way are applied. Each page names its sources.
    </p>

    <h2 class="section-title">A note on Touhou Project</h2>
    <p>
      Touhou Project and its music belong to ZUN and Team Shanghai Alice. This site is an unofficial fan project for
      study and analysis. It does not host any of the original recordings.
    </p>

    <h2 class="section-title">Privacy</h2>
    <p>
      This site has no accounts and does not add analytics or cookies of its own. Your theme choice is kept only in
      your own browser.
    </p>
  </main>
</Layout>
